# Force LF on checkout on every platform.
#
# This working tree is shared across Linux, macOS and Windows by Syncthing, so without this
# a Windows checkout writes CRLF, Syncthing propagates those bytes to the Unix clones, and
# git there reports EVERY tracked file as modified — a phantom whole-tree diff with zero
# content change. retch's v0.4.3 measured exactly that: 13811 insertions / 13811 deletions,
# all line-ending flips, with `git diff --ignore-all-space` empty.
#
# It also overrides Git for Windows' system-level `core.autocrlf = true`, which is why the
# warning "LF will be replaced by CRLF" appears without it. Both sibling repos carry this
# file for the same reason.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be normalised.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text eol=lf
